  "market_context": "The market was in a clear downtrend on the NZD/USD 30-minute chart. A double bottom pattern formed, followed by a downside break of the neckline, setting up a trend continuation short opportunity during the Asian session.",
  "key_observation": "The analyst observed a valid double bottom in a downtrend, with price breaking below the neckline and retesting the lowest candle close as a high-probability short entry zone.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the market direction — confirmed a downtrend on the NZD/USD 30-minute chart.",
    "Step 2: Wait for a valid double bottom formation — two swing lows at approximately the same price, with the second low’s wick touching or exceeding the body of the first low, and the body of the first low not exceeding the wick of the second.",
    "Step 3: Draw a horizontal line at the close of the lowest candle of the double bottom pattern (neckline).",
    "Step 4: Wait for price to retest that line; enter short when a candle closes below the lowest point of the previous candle (rejection confirmation).",
    "Step 5: Place stop loss 1 ATR above the highest point of the rejection candle.",
    "Step 6: Target the next demand area (next structural support level) ahead of price."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "Double bottom patterns are reliable trend continuation signals only when aligned with the dominant trend; precise entry requires candle close confirmation below prior low, and stop placement must respect ATR-based volatility.",
